      "title": "Lead Executive (Project Admin) - Eco-Campus Planning and Development Dept",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] This position will provide the team with specialised document control, digital records governance, and project administration support to the Eco Campus Planning & Development Department. The incumbent will be responsible for establishing, maintaining, and enforcing a robust, compliant, and audit ready digital filing system across SharePoint and the Electronic Records Management System (ERMS) for all projects. The role is targeted at an experienced Document Controller with a strong track record in setting up structured filing systems, enforcing document governance, and ensuring project records are accurate, current, complete, and readily retrievable throughout the project lifecycle. [What you will be working on] Project Document Control & Filing Governance Establish, implement, and maintain a structured, standardised filing system for all Campus Development projects within SharePoint and ERMS. Review, rationalise, and update existing project folders to ensure: Correct document classification and naming conventions Removal of duplicates and obsolete versions Clear version control with the latest approved documents maintained as records Ensure all project documentation (e.g. drawings, reports, submissions, correspondence, approvals, RVOs, RFIs, NCRs, certifications, etc) is: Properly filed Version-controlled Easily retrievable for project, management, or audit purposes Compliance with internal policies, procurement procedures, and public sector governance requirements Conduct periodic document audits to confirm completeness, accuracy, and currency of records. Project Administration & Coordination Support Provide day-to-day administrative and coordination support to EPD, including coordinate project meetings, prepare agendas, tracking and following up on agreed actions, support project close-out activities, including archiving of records and ensuring documentation completeness at handover. Support invoice processing for consultants, contractors, and vendors, including: Verification of supporting documents Cross-checking against contracts, quotations, and approvals Submission through the relevant PO / financial system Maintain accurate records of invoices, payments, and related financial documentation in line with governance and audit requirements. Act as a key point of contact for internal and external audit requests relating to project documentation and financial records. Support responses to audit observations by assisting in document verification and records clarification. Act as a coordination point between internal stakeholders, consultants, contractors and external parties on administrative and documentation matters. Support onboarding, access arrangements and logistics for consultants and project team members. Provide general administrative and secretariat support to EPD as required, including support for management reporting and team coordination. Undertake any other tasks or responsibilities as required by Management in the course of work Identify opportunities to improve document management workflows, filing structures, and administrative processes to enhance efficiency and consistency across projects. Support the development and use of standard templates, trackers, and administrative tools for the EPD. Guide and coordinate administrative processes across multiple projects to ensure consistency and efficiency. [What we are looking for] Relevant qualification in Business Administration, Management or a related discipline. At least 5 years of relevant administrative or executive support experience, preferably in construction industry. Strong organisational skills with the ability to manage multiple tasks and deadlines. Proficient in Microsoft Office applications and comfortable handling documentation and reporting. Prior experience with cloud platform (such as ACONEX, CONJECT, BENTLEY, etc) for managing information and processes for construction and engineering project will be an advantage"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer--Human-Capital-Mgt---Career-Development----Sch-of-Business-Mgt_JR-10000054951": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Human Capital Mgt & Career Development) - Sch of Business Mgt",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-30\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Join the School of Business Management (SBM) to shape future-ready HR professionals through Human Capital Management (HCM), career development, and emerging HR technologies. [What you will be working on] Design, develop and deliver diploma-level learning units in Human Capital Management (HCM) for both pre-employment training (PET) and continuing education and training (CET), using varied modes of delivery such as lectures, tutorials, seminars and e-learning Facilitate engaging learning experiences using industry-relevant, technology-enabled and experiential pedagogies Mentor and guide learners in their holistic development, including career planning, employability skills, internship readiness and professional growth Build and maintain partnerships with employers, industry practitioners and professional bodies to support internships, industry projects and career development initiatives Contribute to programme administration, academic quality assurance, learner development activities and school-wide initiatives [What we are looking for] Relevant qualification in Human Resource Management, or a related discipline At least 5 years of industry experience in HR, career planning, workforce development, or related fields Experience in HR technology, AI, people analytics, or digital transformation initiatives will be an advantage SWDA Certified Career Advisor (CCA) or Certified Career Practitioner (CCP), or experience in career coaching, career counselling, employability development, for young adults and professionals will be an advantage Strong passion for teaching, mentoring, and developing learners for academic and career success. Excellent communication, stakeholder engagement, and facilitation skills, with the ability to work effectively with team members, industry and academic partners"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer--Snr-Lecturer--Brand-Experience-Motion-Design----Sch-of-Design---Media_JR-10000054897": {
      "title": "Lecturer/ Snr Lecturer (Brand Experience Motion Design) – Sch of Design & Media",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Responsible for the design, development and delivery of academically rigorous and industry-relevant teaching in motion branding, motion graphics, visual storytelling, kinetic typography, digital content and brand experience design. The role encompasses curriculum development and enhancement, assessment design, student mentoring and academic advising, industry-integrated learning, and the cultivation of strategic industry partnerships. The position also contributes to applied research, innovation and capability development in emerging creative practices and technologies, while supporting programme administration, quality assurance, outreach and Continuing Education and Training (CET) initiatives. [What you will be working on] Design, develop and deliver lectures, tutorials, studio-based lessons, workshops and asynchronous learning in areas such as motion branding, motion graphics, visual storytelling, kinetic typography, digital content and brand experience design. Develop, review and enhance curriculum, learning resources and assessment strategies to align with programme learning outcomes, industry standards, and evolving needs of the creative industry. Provide mentorship to students on academic performance, portfolio and showreel development, industry opportunities, internships, competitions, further studies and career pathways. Lead and facilitate industry-integrated learning and initiatives , including live briefs, client projects, campaign-based competitions, collaborative productions and industry partnerships. Build and maintain strong relationships with creative agencies, production studios, technology partners, professional bodies and creative networks to strengthen industry relevance, create opportunities for student engagement, and support curriculum development and graduate employability. Contribute to research, innovation and capability development in emerging motion design practices and technologies , including real-time content creation, immersive media , generative AI and other digital tools for creative practice and education. Assist school and programme management and administration , including programme coordination, academic documentation, quality assurance, compliance, outreach and other school-wide initiatives. Support the development and delivery of Continuing Education and Training (CET) or adult learning programmes, particularly in motion branding , digital storytelling and multi-channel brand content, through industry-relevant learning content and professional upskilling initiatives. [What we are looking for] Relevant qualifications with at least five (5) years of professional experience in motion design, motion graphics , brand experience design, visual communication or related creative field. Experience in a leading creative or 4A agency, motion design studio, production house , brand consultancy, digital content company or multinational brand environment will be an advantage. Strong command of motion design principles , visual storytelling, typography, colour, composition and art direction, with a solid understanding of graphic design, 3D visualisation, video production and post-production . Demonstrated ability to develop and maintain high visual standards across digital, physical and experiential brand touchpoints. Practical knowledge of industry-standard design and production tools, such as Adobe After Effects, Premiere Pro , Illustrator, Photoshop, Cinema 4D, Blender , Figma and other relevant other relevant digital, prototyping, motion or content creation platforms. Excellent interpersonal, presentation and communication skills. Prior experience in teaching or mentoring at tertiary or adult-learning level is advantageous. Desirable experience in one or more of the following areas: Motion Branding and Brand Identity Systems Motion Graphics, Animation and Kinetic Typography 2D and 3D Design, Animation and Visualisation Integrated Multi-Channel Brand Campaigns Social Media Content and Digital Storytelling Video Production, Editing and Post-Production Experiential, Immersive or Interactive Media Creative Technology, Generative AI and Emerging Digital Tools"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer---Senior-Lecturer--technopreneurship----School-of-IT_JR-10000054902": {
      "title": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer (Technopreneurship) - School of IT",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] As academic staff, you will play an active role in the academic, professional and personal development of your learners to prepare them for work & life. You will mentor PET and CET learners in transforming IT solutions into viable startup ventures, bridging technical innovation with business success. [What you will be working on] Curriculum & Teaching Design, evaluate, and enhance technopreneurship curricula, and co-develop training content with industry partners and startup ecosystem players Teaching and project supervision of PET and CET courses, including professional short courses in lean startup, business modeling, and IT commercialization Mentor learners through startup development from ideation to market launch, including business planning, customer validation, and pitch preparation Industry Collaboration Spearhead and identify new opportunities, initiatives, and collaborations with VCs, accelerators, incubators, and corporate partners Plan, lead, manage, and undertake IT startup project development with industry and SMEs Guide learners in accessing grants (mentorship Support, ECI, Startup SG) and funding opportunities #LI-Hybrid [What we are looking for] Essential: At least 3 years of experience working in IT relevant job roles.  Relevant qualifications in Computer Science, Engineering, IT, Business, or related fields Good technical background in software development (front-end, back-end, full stack, architecture) Proficiency in traditional AI and generative/agentic AI Proficiency in cloud technologies Strong understanding of startup methodologies, business models, and venture development Good communication and interpersonal skills with ability to connect effectively with diverse learners Good to have: Track record in fundraising, scaling startups, or bringing tech products to market Network within Singapore's startup ecosystem and familiarity with local funding landscape Prior teaching or mentoring experience in entrepreneurship Entrepreneurial mindset with practical, hands-on approach"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer-Senior-Lecturer--Cloud-Computing----School-of-Engineering_JR-10000049061": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Cloud Engineering) – School of Engineering",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] This is a full-time Lecturer/Senior Lecturer position focused on delivering high-quality education in Cloud Engineering. The role involves teaching and mentoring learners in areas such as cloud engineering, cloud-native application development, DevOps and emerging technologies. The successful candidate will deliver applied and experiential learning, mentor students in developing and deployment of scalable, secure and production-ready cloud solutioning aligned with industry needs. Candidates with experience or interest in Artificial Intelligence (AI), Internet of Things (IoT), cloud-enabled digital transformation initiatives will an added advantage. [What you will be working on] The successful candidate will: Develop and deliver learning units in the following areas Cloud Engineering & Cloud Native Development: Design and development of cloud-native applications and services using languages such as Python, JavaScript, APIs, SDKs, microservices and managed cloud services. DevOps & Platform Engineering & Automation: Implementation of CI/CD pipelines, Infrastructure as Code (IaC), containerisations, monitoring and automated deployment practices. Emerging Cloud Technologies : Adoption and application of AI, Generative AI, Data Analytics, IoT and other digital technologies within cloud environments. Develop and deliver industry-relevant curriculum, assessments and experiential learning activities Supervise student projects and provide guidance aligned with industry practices Participate in curriculum development, academic quality processes and continuous improvement initiatives Stay abreast of industry trends by participating or initiating in the development of industry-relevant projects and integrating emerging technologies into teaching and learning [What we are looking for] We are seeking a candidate who possesses: Relevant academic qualifications in Computer Engineering, Information System, Computer Science, Cloud Computing or a related field. Practical knowledge and hands-on experience in cloud-native application development, DevOps practices or platform engineering. Proficiency in programming and scripting languages such as Python and JavaScript, with experience in developing applications and integrating cloud services through APIs and SDKs. Strong communication skills, with a genuine passion for teaching, mentoring and engaging learners. Experience or interest in Artificial Intelligence (AI), Internet of Things (IoT), cloud-enabled digital transformation initiatives will be considered a plus. Relevant cloud certifications (e.g., AWS, Azure, etc) will be an advantage. #LI-Hybrid"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer--Business-Communication----Sch-of-Business-Mgt_JR-10000054834": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Business Communication) - Sch of Business Mgt",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] We are seeking educators and industry practitioners who are passionate about developing learners' workplace communication, professional presence, and digital communication capabilities. The role contributes to the preparation of adaptable communicators who can thrive in increasingly technology-enabled and AI-enhanced workplace environments. Join us in shaping the future of communication education by empowering learners with the communication, digital, and AI fluency needed to thrive in a rapidly evolving world. [What you will be working on] Teaching and facilitating learning across Polytechnic Foundation Programme (PFP) , Pre-Employment Training ( PET ), and Continuing Education & Training ( CET ) programmes through classroom delivery, assessment, consultation, project supervision, and learner support. Designing, developing, and reviewing curriculum, learning activities, and assessments to ensure alignment with industry practices, workplace communication needs, and educational best practices for both PET and CET. Developing learners' communication competencies in areas such as business writing, presentations, digital communication, content creation, stakeholder engagement, professional branding, and workplace communication. Integrating Generative AI (GenAI), digital technologies, and innovative pedagogies into teaching and assessment, while developing learners' competencies in AI-assisted communication, responsible AI use, critical evaluation, and human-AI collaboration . Collaborating with industry partners, professional bodies, and other stakeholders to co-create authentic learning experiences, communication projects, and innovative training initiatives. Mentoring and supporting the academic, professional, and personal development of youth and adult learners through inclusive, learner-centred, and adaptive teaching approaches. Contributing to industry engagement, professional development, outreach activities, school initiatives, committee work, and administrative responsibilities. [What we are looking for] A relevant qualification in Communication Studies, Mass Communication, Corporate Communication, Strategic Communication, Marketing Communication, Applied Linguistics, Education, or a related discipline. At least 3 years of relevant industry and/or teaching experience in communication, content development, training, education, digital communication, marketing communication, or related fields. Familiarity with AI, digital technologies, and emerging communication trends, with the ability to apply these effectively in professional or educational settings. Experience in curriculum development, teaching, facilitation, coaching, training, or adult learning. Experience in CET, corporate training, or workforce development will be an advantage. Strong communication, facilitation, presentation, interpersonal, and stakeholder engagement skills. Ability to develop learner-centred learning experiences that foster communication competence, critical thinking, digital fluency, and responsible use of technology. Passion for learner development, with strong organisational skills, adaptability, and the ability to manage multiple responsibilities effectively."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer-Snr-Lecturer--Biomedical-Science-with-Analytics----Sch-of-Applied-Sc_JR-10000054658": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Snr Lecturer (Biomedical Science with Analytics) - Sch of Applied Sc",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 20 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] You will play an active role in the academic, professional, and personal development of the learners to prepare them for work and life. This includes development of Pre-Employment Training (PET) and Continuing Education & Training (CET) curriculum, programme delivery and working on industry projects. [What you will be working on] Develop, deliver and review PET and CET curriculum, including face-to-face, online and blended learning. Design and develop teaching materials, assessments, applied projects and authentic learning activities that include integrating science with AI and data analytics. Prepare and grade assessments and supervise learners in their daily course work. Use the Learning Management System and interactive digital tools effectively, and harness technology to enhance learner engagement and outcomes. Serve as a Personal Mentor to learners, providing pastoral support and assisting with day-to-day academic and administrative matters. Contribute to school and diploma-level initiatives, committee work, outreach activities, curriculum reviews and quality assurance processes. Build and maintain strong partnerships with industry to lead and develop industry projects, internships and collaborative initiatives. #LI-Hybrid [What we are looking for] Highly motivated, resourceful and learner-centric candidates who are nurturing and enjoy interacting with learners with the following: Relevant qualifications in Biomedical Science/Life Sciences, with expertise in Clinical Laboratory Sciences and qualifications or experience in Bioinformatics, Data Analytics, Data Science or related disciplines. Minimum 3 years of relevant work experience in a science related field. Demonstrated experience applying AI, machine learning, predictive analytics or modelling to solve real-world biomedical, healthcare or life sciences problems. Proficient in analytics tools or programming languages such as SAS Viya, Python, SQL, Power BI or equivalent. Strong communication, interpersonal and mentoring skills, with the ability to collaborate effectively, adapt to changing needs and manage multiple priorities. Candidates are also expected to contribute to teaching and curriculum development in one or more of the following areas: Predictive Analytics & Forecasting, Predictive Modelling, Database Design & Administration, Data & Statistical methods and Applied Calculus."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer--Human-Centred-Design-for-AI---Cloud-Innovation----School-of-Engineering_JR-10000054620": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Human-Centred Design for AI & Cloud Innovation) – School of Engineering",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 20 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] This is a full-time Lecturer position focused on delivering high-quality education in Human-Centred Design for AI & Cloud Innovation. The role involves teaching and mentoring learners in design thinking, human-centred design, innovation methodologies, product development, prototyping and technology-driven solutioning. [What you will be working on] The successful candidate will develop and deliver learning units in: Design thinking, human-centred design and innovation Product design, prototyping, testing, validation and iterative development Engineering problem-solving, systems thinking and solution development Innovation management, entrepreneurship, and technobusiness Sustainable, user-centric and impactful design practices Apply cloud, AI, IoT and emerging technologies to engineering design and innovation Integrate relevant digital tools/technologies and expose learners to smart, connected and technology-enabled solutions Develop industry-relevant curriculum, assessments and experiential learning activities Supervise student projects, innovation challenges and industry-based projects Mentor learners in design thinking, innovation, entrepreneurship & product development Build industry partnerships to support applied learning, innovation and capability development Stay current with emerging trends/developments and integrate them into teaching [What we are looking for] We are seeking a candidate with: Relevant qualifications in Engineering, Design Engineering, Product Design, Innovation, Computer Engineering, Information Systems or related fields. 3–5 years of relevant industry or practical experience in engineering design, product development, innovation or technology-enabled solutions. Experience in design thinking, prototyping, user-centred design, innovation and project-based learning. Familiarity with cloud platforms, digital technologies or smart systems; experience in AI, IoT, automation, digital twins or data analytics is preferred. Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with a passion for teaching and mentoring. Experience in industry projects, innovation initiatives and product development will be an advantage. Relevant professional certifications in engineering, innovation, design, cloud technologies or project management will be beneficial. #LI-Hybrid"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/NYP-CIL3/Lead-Executive-Asst-Manager--IP-management----Centre-for-Industry---Lifelong-Learning_JR-10000052328": {
      "title": "Lead Executive/Asst Manager (IP management) - Centre for Industry & Lifelong Learning",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-19\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] The individual supports the administration and management of applied research activities across IP protection, licensing, Technology Transfer, and grants management. The role involves maintaining accurate IP records and filing documentation, supporting licensing and deal closure processes, coordinating grant submissions and post-award administration, and liaising with internal and external stakeholders on related financial, legal, and business matters. The individual also contributes to the department's digitalisation initiatives, data analytics, and broader administrative and project work. [What you will be working on] The individual will support the administration and management of applied research activities, spanning IP protection, IP management processes, licensing, and grants management. Key responsibilities include:   IP Management & Protection Supporting the administration and reporting of applied research outputs, including patents and other forms of IP, in accordance with established processes and SOPs. Performing IP-related searches and maintaining accurate filing records, registers, and repositories with proper version control. Preparing standard IP-related documents such as NDAs, assignments, and confidentiality undertakings, and routing them for the necessary approvals. Tracking filing deadlines, prosecution timelines, and patent expenses, and preparing utilisation reports for management review. Escalating IP-related concerns such as novelty and confidentiality issues promptly to senior staff.   IP Licensing & Technology Transfer Supporting licensing and Technology Transfer activities, including the preparation of standard collaterals and coordination of deal closure processes. Maintaining an industry contacts database and opportunities pipeline, and providing support for IP marketing activities such as exhibitions, trade shows, workshops, and seminars. Liaising with internal and external stakeholders on licensing and Technology Transfer matters, including financial, legal, and business aspects. Handling billing processes and coordinating with external IP holders to facilitate payment for licensing deals.   Grants & Project Administration Tracking funding calls and deadlines, sourcing relevant grant opportunities, and maintaining a grants calendar and pipeline tracker. Performing basic eligibility screening for grant opportunities and coordinating post-award setup activities including project codes, reporting schedules, and document packs. Working with NYP Schools and funding agencies on industry project submissions, grants administration, and Continuing Education and Training (CET) programmes. Tracking and analysing data across grants management, funding utilisation, licensing activities, and other key performance indicators for reporting to relevant agencies. General Supporting the department's digitalisation initiatives and data analytics. Providing broad administrative and management support across departmental functions. Contributing to committees and cross-functional project work as required #Li-Hybrid [What we are looking for] Meticulous and driven individual to support our Technology Transfer Office in managing end-to-end IP and grants administration. Relevant qualifications in Engineering or Life Sciences, is comfortable working with data, and can manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Strong team player with good communication and interpersonal skills, and be able to liaise effectively with a diverse range of internal and external stakeholders. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications is essential, and prior knowledge of IP, Technology Transfer, or grants management is preferred. Experience in, or a demonstrated interest in, digitalisation and data analytics to drive improvements in work processes would be highly valued."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/NYP-FN/Senior-Executive--Finance_JR-10000054042": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Finance",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] The Senior Executive, Finance is responsible for supporting Accounts Receivable (AR) operations across various business portfolios, including billing, collections, debt management, account reconciliation and stakeholder support. The role works closely with internal and external stakeholders to ensure accurate and timely financial processing, effective revenue collection, compliance with financial policies and continuous improvement of finance operations. [What you will be working on] What You Will Be Working On Manage Accounts Receivable (AR) functions, including billing, collections, debt management, account maintenance, adjustments and refunds. Process and maintain billing activities for various revenue streams, such as projects, rentals, student accommodation, Continuing Education and Training (CET) programmes and miscellaneous adhoc billings. Monitor outstanding receivables and coordinate with stakeholders to facilitate timely collection of debts. Perform account reconciliations and prepare reports to ensure the accuracy and completeness of financial records. Analyse financial and operational data to identify trends, exceptions and areas requiring follow-up. Liaise with internal and external stakeholders to resolve billing, payment, refund and account-related matters. Ensure compliance with financial policies, procedures, internal controls and audit requirements. Maintain accurate documentation and records to support operational, reporting and governance requirements. #LI-Hybrid [What we are looking for] Additional Responsibilities Review and enhance work processes through streamlining, digitalisation and automation initiatives to improve operational efficiency and service delivery. Support the implementation, enhancement and testing of finance systems and related applications. Participate in finance-related projects, process improvement initiatives and transformation efforts. Provide guidance and support to users on finance-related processes and systems. Collaborate with Schools, Departments and stakeholders to support organisational objectives and operational requirements. Contribute to continuous improvement and knowledge-sharing within the Finance Department. Perform any other duties and responsibilities as assigned. What We Are Looking For Qualifications in Accountancy, Finance, Business Administration or a related discipline. Relevant working experience in Accounts Receivable, billing, collections, finance operations or shared services environment. Good understanding of accounting principles, financial controls and receivables management processes. Strong analytical, problem-solving and organisational skills. Proficient in Microsoft Office applications, particularly Excel. Experience with Workday and STEP is preferred. Good communication and stakeholder management skills. Meticulous, customer-focused and able to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Proactive team player with a continuous improvement mindset and interest in process optimisation and digitalisation."
    },
